        "vid": "07e99f22-c176-4c8f-9678-a57ba8114959"
    },
    "details": "Helder Eijs reports\n\n> Fix timing leaks of the nonce in ECDSA, EdDSA and DSA signatures The\n> signing time depended on the secret nonce, enough to recover the\n> private key with a lattice attack. - EC: scalars are encoded and\n> processed on the full length of the order, and ec_mix_add() is\n> constant time for the point at infinity (a zero digit). - DSA: g\\^k\n> uses k + q or k + 2q (fixed length) and mpz_powm_sec, or the\n> library\\'s Montgomery exponentiation without GMP. About 40% slower.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0510",
    "modified": "2026-10-12T00:00:00Z",
    "published": "2026-10-12T00:00:00Z",
